course: dictionary
lesson: 6625
title: What a notebook means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which one is meant. «After a year of zoo visits, the notebook is full: big cats, apes, reptiles, birds, frogs and insects.» A notebook that holds pictures and notes about animals is a small book with empty pages for writing.
explain: Look for clues that point to the other meaning. A notebook can also be a small, light laptop computer. Words like screen, battery or typing would show you that meaning. Here the sentence has no screen, so the book meaning fits.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «He called the notebook «the book of truth».» Put in a small book and it still makes sense. Put in a laptop and it sounds odd, so the book meaning is the right one.
fact: A notebook is a small book with empty pages for writing.
fact: A notebook can also be a small, light laptop computer.
fact: Notebook is a noun, and its plural is notebooks.
fact: Careful notes let other people check and compare, as «Charles Darwin filled notebooks on his round-the-world voyage on the ship Beagle» shows.
fact: A good check for any word with two meanings is to swap each meaning into the sentence and see which one still makes sense.
exercise: «After a year of zoo visits, the notebook is full of animal facts.» What is the notebook here? | A small, light laptop with a screen | A zoo keeper who feeds the animals | *A small book with empty pages for writing | A big cat with spots
exercise: What is the plural of notebook? | notebook-s | *notebooks | notebooky | notebookes
exercise: «Two days later she asks him, Do you like drawing? He shows her a notebook of amazing robots.» What does the notebook hold? | A map of the moon | A list of train times | A recipe for soup | *Drawings of robots
test: Which is a second meaning of notebook? | A kind of bicycle | *A small, light laptop computer | A cup for hot drinks | A tall, thin plant
test: In «He called the notebook «the book of truth»», what does the phrase suggest the notebook is? | A tent | *A book | A pencil case | A bus
exam: Mum buys 3 notebooks at 2 pounds each. How much does she pay altogether? | 8 pounds | *6 pounds | 5 pounds | 3 pounds
